/* carrierdrop.apt
**
** $VER: carrierdrop.apt 0.0.1 (2.3.93)
**
** ARexx program for controlling ApT-BBS by ApT-Design.
**
** As this file will only ever be used when we are sure that a user has first
** had his account loaded into the system (after giving the correct password)
** we can be safe in knowing that we have a 'valid' account to do something
** with. Obviously as the line has been already 'cut' it  would be rather
** silly to even attempt to send out a message to the screen, besides,
** most of the the display commands would return back without doing anything
** if the line has been dropped. You are however still able to do a number
** of tasks to the users account etc..
**
** Copyright © 1993 ApT-Design All Rights Reserved,AG
**
*/

BYTESLEFT_VAR		= 9

parse arg lineno
options results

portname = 'APTREXX'lineno
address value portname

/*
**
** As the user has dropped carrier lets alert him of this
** and remove around 10K from his account.
**
*/

'ALERTLOG' "Dropped carrier - Please try to log off without cutting the line!!"

/* Temp disabled drop fine!!
*
* 'GETVAR' BYTESLEFT_VAR
* bytesleft = result - 10240
* 'SETVAR' BYTESLEFT_VAR bytesleft
* 'FLUSHACCOUNT'
* 'ALERTLOG' "10K of bytes removed as a penalty for carrier drop."
*/



/*
** Incase a user dropped carrier when the 'module/sample player'
** was in action we should always makesure that the sound is
** turned off in this instance.
*/

/* address 'RXTRACKER' 'UNLOAD' */

'APTXEND'
EXIT

